# Quick Start

Get Nocturne up and running in just a few minutes.

## Prerequisites

Before you begin, make sure you have:

- Docker and Docker Compose installed
- A server or VPS with at least 1 GB RAM
- A domain name (recommended) or static IP

## Step 1: Create your project

```
mkdir nocturne && cd nocturne
```

## Step 2: Deploy

Follow one of our [installation guides](/docs/installation) to set up the Docker Compose stack and configure your environment variables.

## Step 3: Access Your Instance

Once the containers are running, access your Nocturne instance at:

```
https://your-server-ip:8443
```

Sign in and you land on the home screen. It stays empty until a device or an app
starts sending readings:

<Screenshot id="first-run" />

## Step 4: Connect a data source

Open **Settings > Data Sources**. Every service Nocturne can collect readings
from, and every phone app that can send readings to it, is listed as a tile:

<Screenshot id="connect-data-source" />

Pick the one your readings come from and fill in what it asks for — for Dexcom,
that is the username and password of the Dexcom Share account you already use.
Turn the connection on and Nocturne starts collecting on its own.

<Screenshot
  id="connector-dexcom"
  callouts={[
    { anchor: "enable-switch", label: "Turn the connection on" },
    { anchor: "credentials", label: "Enter your Dexcom Share sign-in" },
  ]}
/>

